From ebe4e243e88981dda24b287d3c5db9928dca1b83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:08:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] NGAP: decode and answer the multicast MBS procedures of a
 join

When a UE joins a multicast MBS session, two things reach the gNB over N2 that
it did not understand: a per-UE PDU Session Resource Modify carrying the MBS
session the UE's PDU session is now associated with, and a non-UE-associated
Multicast Session Activation for that session. The first had its MBS IE
dropped with "Unhandled optional IE"; the second had no handler at all and was
discarded by the dispatcher.

- decodePDUSessionResourceModify() now reads
  id-MBSSessionSetuporModifyRequestList (TS 38.413 V17.10.0, ProtocolIE-ID 319)
  into the modify request, and ngap_gNB_pdusession_modify_resp() answers with
  id-MBSSessionSetuporModifyResponseList (313) and id-MBS-SupportIndicator,
  both extensions of PDUSessionResourceModifyResponseTransfer. TS 23.247
  V18.8.0 clause 7.2.1.3 step 9: "If the MBS is supported by NG-RAN, the N2 SM
  information further includes the indication of supporting MBS."

- ngap_gNB_handle_multicast_session_activation() handles procedure code 71
  (TS 38.413 clause 8.18.3). It records that the core wants the session on and
  answers a MULTICAST SESSION ACTIVATION RESPONSE naming the session the
  request was fulfilled for, or a FAILURE with a cause when it cannot take it.
  Activating the radio is not built yet; answering the procedure correctly is.

The NAS PDU of a modify item is optional (clause 9.2.1.5) while the transfer is
not, so the transfer is now decoded whether or not a NAS PDU came with it --
an MBS join carries both, but a modify with only the MBS list is well formed
and used to be skipped entirely.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PR4cGwmGjgMjM39K5jaxnP
